From: the jellyfin-ffmpeg contributors
Subject: backport a fix for pts overflow in deint vaapi filter
Origin: https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg/blob/v8.1.3-2/debian/patches/0103-backport-a-fix-for-pts-overflow-in-deint-vaapi-filter.patch

deinterlace_vaapi keeps the last timestamp in 64 bits.

Rebased onto FFmpeg 9.0.2: the same change, at 9.0.2's line numbers.

From jellyfin-ffmpeg 8.1.3-2, where the patch has no header: its authors
are in that repository's history. Under FFmpeg's licence, as the files
it changes.
---
diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_vaapi.c b/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_vaapi.c
--- a/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_vaapi.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_vaapi.c
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ typedef struct DeintVAAPIContext {
     int                extra_delay_for_timestamps;
 
     int                eof;
-    int                prev_pts;
+    int64_t            prev_pts;
 } DeintVAAPIContext;
 
 static const char *deint_vaapi_mode_name(int mode)
